  "HOLD absence of a released patch as sufficient zero-day evidence. Newly discovered does not specify discovery-time vendor/defender unknownness; the retained keyed option still asserts zero-day while the main feedback only establishes patch unavailability. Prior m130/m613 unknown-flaw qualifications remain; do not turn lack of a fix into unknownness or failed patching. HOLD exact whole 2.5 assessed scope: this asks what a gap illustrates rather than selecting or explaining a particular enterprise mitigation; retain patching-limit context without forcing 2.3. Suggested isolation/least privilege/monitoring may reduce exposure, not universally address the flaw or demonstrate a defense. No actual exploit, vendor notice, fix, isolation, protection or remedy is observed.",
  "HOLD firewall rules as preventing all pivoting, access or escalation, port-only allow rules as sufficient, and required application traffic as automatically safe. The current stem limits other paths while expressly preserving one application connection. Source/destination/service restrictions and application/database authorisation remain separate needs. The authored cannot-reach-DB guarantee is superseded. AV, authentication and logging can contribute but are not the offered path-policy mechanism; controls can be combined. One rule choice supplies no independent source, destination, port or database-permission components. Correlate with m133 general segmentation; no firewall, request, compromise containment or prevention is implemented.",
  "HOLD Base64 alone as SQL injection, every application/WAF as decoding every encoding automatically, normalisation as universal prevention or a product-category swap as guaranteed parsing parity. The effective stem explicitly supplies application decoding and WAF raw-field inspection mismatch; authored generic encoded-bypass and raw-input-is-trivially-bypassed claims are superseded. Align field scope, order, character handling and bounded transformations with actual application semantics and test; do not arbitrarily decode all inputs. Current main teaching names parameterised queries as remediation context, not an assessed implemented defense or independent SQL skill. Preserve prior SQL/query, WAF/NGFW/TLS visibility and input-boundary holds. No input, payload, decoder, query, firewall or attack executes.",
  "HOLD spoofed addresses as unique host/actor counts, SYN cookies as blocking volumetric link saturation, authentication of a benign peer, zero server processing cost, or universal safe handling of every TCP option/stack. Cookies delay full per-connection state until a validated handshake completion; some implementation work/resources remain. Current main feedback corrects the authored zero-memory shorthand. Longer half-open timeouts can prolong pressure; blocking all TCP conflicts with legitimate TCP availability; an IDS may drive a separate response but passive sensing alone does not enforce this mitigation. No packets, cookie, backlog, platform configuration, outage or recovery is measured; preserve DDoS/freshness qualifications.",
  "HOLD minimum permission scope as an implemented guarantee of safe access, every role definition as accurate, and separation of duties as never restricting permissions. The retained SoD correction says it does not restrict permission scope and reduces it to multiple people completing a process; static conflicting-role restrictions can implement it. Hold that precise contrast while retaining minimum task access as the offered principle. MAC labels can enforce access consistent with least privilege; MAC acronym/network-address polysemy must not force another canonical concept. Job rotation can affect role assignments but is not the minimum-scope principle. Correlate closely with m113; no entitlements, account, fraud reduction or compromise impact is tested.",
  "HOLD job title/seniority as sufficient required permissions, all users as forbidden any justified administrative task, request approval as least privilege by itself or reduced compromise damage as measured. Minimum actual task/function scope is the supplied principle; correct role definitions, enforcement and changing duties still require review. An approval workflow can support governance and temporary privilege without defining the minimum necessary rights. Authored domain 1 is superseded by effective domain 2/objective 2.5. Correlate closely with m014, with no approved family independence, live permission check or prevention/recovery outcome.",
  "HOLD subnet/VLAN separation alone as enforced isolation, every segmented network as eliminating lateral movement, NAT as a universal security boundary, or QoS/throttling as unable to drop traffic under any policy. Current main explicitly requires enforced rules. Performance controls can shape/drop traffic but do not by themselves implement the offered zone-authorisation policy. Correlate with m138 which preserves a required path, without granting independent family/component evidence. No topology, rule, segmentation rollout, route, throughput, intrusion or movement is measured.",
  "HOLD DEP/NX as necessarily implementing strict writable-XOR-executable policy, eliminating buffer corruption/code reuse, protecting every process/configuration or establishing that injected data was present/executed. The supplied protected-page mechanism is meaningful; NX hardware and OS/page-permission policy cooperate. Current main corrects the authored not-both-writable-and-executable guarantee. ASLR, canaries and CFG address different limited mechanisms and may combine; none is separately keyed evidence. DEP is inferred general hardening context, not a named 2.5 bullet, and authored domain 3 is superseded. No memory permissions, exploit, bypass, CPU or installed protection is tested.",
  "HOLD removal as eliminating every host risk, disabling as identical to uninstalling, all legacy-protocol deployments as identical cleartext configurations or TLS retrofit as automatically safe. The fictional stem declares no production need; current main adds dependency/change checks. ACLs, encryption and segmentation can help required services, but retaining these stipulated unused services preserves exposure/maintenance. One combined disable/remove choice supplies no separately observed decommissioning actions. No live process, package, dependency, change, service removal, network test or residual exposure is measured; preserve TLS/access/product and remediation qualifications."
